#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:80
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "简介"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:82
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Major and Minor Versions"
msgstr "主要版本和次要版本"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:86
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Since FreeBSD 6.0-RELEASE, FreeBSD releases have adhered strictly to a two-"
"level numbering scheme.  We use the term “major version” to describe the "
"first part of the version number, e.g. the “14” in “14.3-RELEASE”, and the "
"term “minor version” to describe the second part of the version number, e.g. "
"the “3” in “14.3-RELEASE”."
msgstr "从 FreeBSD 6.0-RELEASE 开始，FreeBSD 发行版严格遵循两级编号方案。我们使用“主要版本”一词来描述版本号的第一部分，例如“14.3-RELEASE”中的“14”；使用“次要版本”一词来描述版本号的第二部分，例如“14.3-RELEASE”中的“3”。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:88
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Additionally, FreeBSD release branches have a patch level, which is omitted "
"when zero and incremented with every batch of security advisories and errata "
"notices, e.g. “14.3-RELEASE-p7” for the seventh batch of patches published "
"for FreeBSD 14.3."
msgstr "此外，FreeBSD 发行分支还有一个补丁级别；级别为零时会省略该数字，每批安全公告和勘误通知发布后，该级别都会递增。例如，针对 FreeBSD 14.3 发布的第七批补丁版本为“14.3-RELEASE-p7”。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:91
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"As a consequence of the https://www.FreeBSD.org/security/#model[FreeBSD "
"support model], FreeBSD version numbers increase monotonically within the "
"same major version, but not across different major versions.  For instance, "
"FreeBSD 14.2-RELEASE, 13.5-RELEASE, 14.3-RELEASE, 15.0-RELEASE, 14.4-"
"RELEASE, and 15.1-RELEASE were released in that order."
msgstr "根据 link:https://www.FreeBSD.org/security/#model[FreeBSD 支持模式]，FreeBSD 版本号在同一个主要版本内单调递增，但在不同主要版本之间不遵循此规律。例如，FreeBSD 14.2-RELEASE、13.5-RELEASE、14.3-RELEASE、15.0-RELEASE、14.4-RELEASE 和 15.1-RELEASE 按此顺序发布。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:92
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Updating and Upgrading FreeBSD"
msgid "Updating vs. Upgrading"
msgstr "更新与升级 FreeBSD"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:95
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We use the term “updating” to describe applying security or errata patches "
"which may increment the patch level but do not increment the version number, "
"and the term “upgrading” to describe replacing the entire base system with "
"one with a different version number."
msgstr "我们使用“更新”一词来描述应用安全补丁或勘误补丁的过程；此过程可能会提高补丁级别，但不会增加版本号。我们使用“升级”一词来描述将整个基本系统替换为不同版本号的系统。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:96
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Upgrade Paths"
msgstr "升级路径"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:100
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once installed, FreeBSD may be updated or upgraded using crossref:cutting-"
"edge[updating-upgrading-freebsdupdate,binary patches], crossref:cutting-"
"edge[pkgbase,packages], or crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld,from source].  In "
"all cases FreeBSD only supports updating or upgrading from a chronologically "
"older version to a more recent one."
msgstr "安装后，可以使用 crossref:cutting-edge[updating-upgrading-freebsdupdate,二进制补丁]、crossref:cutting-edge[pkgbase,软件包] 或 crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld,从源代码构建] 更新或升级 FreeBSD。所有情况下，FreeBSD 仅支持从时间上较早的版本更新或升级到较新的版本。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:103
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Specifically, FreeBSD supports updating to a more recent patch level of the "
"same version, or upgrading from a given version to either a more recent "
"minor version of the same major version (e.g. from 14.3 to 14.4) or to a "
"more recent version of the next major version (e.g. from 14.3 to 15.0 or "
"15.1).  Moving to an older release of the same major version (e.g. from 14.4 "
"to 14.3), to an older release of the next major version (e.g. from 14.4, "
"released in March 2026, to 15.0, released three months earlier in December "
"2025), or skipping a major version (e.g. from 13.5 to 15.1) is neither "
"recommended nor supported, even if the tools allow it."
msgstr "具体而言，FreeBSD 支持更新到同一版本的较高补丁级别，也支持从指定版本升级到同一主要版本中较新的次要版本（例如从 14.3 升级到 14.4），或升级到下一个主要版本中较新的版本（例如从 14.3 升级到 15.0 或 15.1）。迁移到同一主要版本中较旧的发行版（例如从 14.4 降级到 14.3）、迁移到下一个主要版本中较旧的发行版（例如从 2026 年 3 月发布的 14.4 升级到三个月前，即 2025 年 12 月发布的 15.0），或跳过一个主要版本（例如从 13.5 升级到 15.1）均不受支持，也不建议这样做，即使相关工具允许操作。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "FreeBSD Update"
msgstr "FreeBSD更新"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:109
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Applying security patches in a timely manner and upgrading to a newer "
"release of an operating system are important aspects of ongoing system "
"administration.  FreeBSD includes a utility called `freebsd-update` which "
"can be used to perform both these tasks."
msgstr ""
"随时套用安全性更新以及升级到新发布的操作系统版本对管理一个持续运作的系统是非"
"常重要的任务，FreeBSD内含可以执行这两项任务的工具程序，叫做<command>freebsd-"
"update</command>。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:113
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This utility supports binary security and errata updates to FreeBSD, without "
"the need to manually compile and install the patch or a new kernel.  Binary "
"updates are available for all architectures and releases currently supported "
"by the security team.  The list of supported releases and their estimated "
"end-of-life dates are listed at https://www.FreeBSD.org/security/[https://"
"www.FreeBSD.org/security/]."
msgstr "此工具支持对 FreeBSD 应用二进制安全更新和勘误更新，无需手动编译和安装补丁或新内核。所有安全团队当前支持的架构和发行版都提供二进制更新。受支持的发行版及其预计停止支持日期列于 link:https://www.FreeBSD.org/security/[https://www.FreeBSD.org/security/]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:117
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This utility also supports operating system upgrades to minor point releases "
"as well as upgrades to another release branch.  Before upgrading to a new "
"release, review its release announcement as it contains important "
"information pertinent to the release.  Release announcements are available "
"from https://www.FreeBSD.org/releases/[https://www.FreeBSD.org/releases/]."
msgstr "此工具还支持将操作系统升级到次要点发行版，以及升级到其他发行分支。升级到新发行版之前，请查看其发行公告，因为其中包含与该发行版相关的重要信息。发行公告可在 link:https://www.FreeBSD.org/releases/[https://www.FreeBSD.org/releases/] 获取。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:121
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If a man:crontab[5] utilizing the features of man:freebsd-update[8] exists, "
"it must be disabled before upgrading the operating system."
msgstr "如果存在使用 man:freebsd-update[8] 功能的 man:crontab[5]，必须在升级操作系统之前将其禁用。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:124
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This section describes the configuration file used by `freebsd-update`, "
"demonstrates how to apply a security patch and how to upgrade to a minor or "
"major operating system release, and discusses some of the considerations "
"when upgrading the operating system."
msgstr ""
"本节将说明<command>freebsd-update</command>使用的配置文件，示范如何套用安全性"
"修补及如何升级到主要或次要的操作系统发行版，并讨论升级操作系统的需要考察的事"
"项。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Configuration File"
msgstr "配置文件"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:131
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The default configuration file for `freebsd-update` works as-is.  Some users "
"may wish to tweak the default configuration in [.filename]#/etc/freebsd-"
"update.conf#, allowing better control of the process.  The comments in this "
"file explain the available options, but the following may require a bit more "
"explanation:"
msgstr ""
"<command>freebsd-update</command>预设的配置文件不需变更即可运作。部份使用者可"
"能会想要调校位于<filename>/etc/freebsd-update.conf</filename>的预设配置文件来"
"对程序有更好的控制。该配置文件中的注释均有说明可用的选项，但以下几个项目可能"
"需要进一步的说明："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:136
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Components of the base system which should be kept updated.\n"
"Components world kernel\n"
msgstr ""
"# Components of the base system which should be kept updated.\n"
"Components world kernel\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:143
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This parameter controls which parts of FreeBSD will be kept up-to-date.  The "
"default is to update the entire base system and the kernel.  Individual "
"components can instead be specified, such as `src/base` or `src/sys`.  "
"However, the best option is to leave this at the default as changing it to "
"include specific items requires every needed item to be listed.  Over time, "
"this could have disastrous consequences as source code and binaries may "
"become out of sync."
msgstr ""
"这个参数控制FreeBSD要保持最新版本的部份。预设是更新整个基础系统（Base "
"system）和核心。可指定个别元件，例如：<literal>src/base</literal>或"
"<literal>src/sys</literal>。虽然如此，最好的选项是维持预设值，因为更改指定特"
"定项目时需列出每一个需要的项目。时间一久可能会因为源码和Binary文件没有更新而"
"造成惨重的后果。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:149
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Paths which start with anything matching an entry in an IgnorePaths\n"
"# statement will be ignored.\n"
"IgnorePaths /boot/kernel/linker.hints\n"
msgstr ""
"# Paths which start with anything matching an entry in an IgnorePaths\n"
"# statement will be ignored.\n"
"IgnorePaths /boot/kernel/linker.hints\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:153
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To leave specified directories, such as [.filename]#/bin# or [.filename]#/"
"sbin#, untouched during the update process, add their paths to this "
"statement.  This option may be used to prevent `freebsd-update` from "
"overwriting local modifications."
msgstr ""
"要保持特定的目录在更新过程不被更动，例如<filename>/bin</filename>或"
"<filename>/sbin</filename>，可以将他们的路径加到此叙述中。这个选项可以防止"
"<command>freebsd-update</command>覆盖本地的修改。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:160
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Paths which start with anything matching an entry in an UpdateIfUnmodified\n"
"# statement will only be updated if the contents of the file have not been\n"
"# modified by the user (unless changes are merged; see below).\n"
"UpdateIfUnmodified /etc/ /var/ /root/ /.cshrc /.profile\n"
msgstr ""
"# Paths which start with anything matching an entry in an UpdateIfUnmodified\n"
"# statement will only be updated if the contents of the file have not been\n"
"# modified by the user (unless changes are merged; see below).\n"
"UpdateIfUnmodified /etc/ /var/ /root/ /.cshrc /.profile\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:165
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This option will only update unmodified configuration files in the specified "
"directories.  Any changes made by the user will prevent the automatic "
"updating of these files.  There is another option, `KeepModifiedMetadata`, "
"which will instruct `freebsd-update` to save the changes during the merge."
msgstr "此选项只会更新指定目录中未修改的配置文件。用户所做的任何更改都会阻止这些文件自动更新。另有一个选项 `KeepModifiedMetadata`，可指示 `freebsd-update` 在合并过程中保存这些更改。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:171
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# When upgrading to a new FreeBSD release, files which match MergeChanges\n"
"# will have any local changes merged into the version from the new release.\n"
"MergeChanges /etc/ /var/named/etc/ /boot/device.hints\n"
msgstr ""
"# When upgrading to a new FreeBSD release, files which match MergeChanges\n"
"# will have any local changes merged into the version from the new release.\n"
"MergeChanges /etc/ /var/named/etc/ /boot/device.hints\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:177
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"List of directories with configuration files that `freebsd-update` should "
"attempt to merge.  The file merge process is a series of man:diff[1] "
"patches.  Merges are either accepted, open an editor, or cause `freebsd-"
"update` to abort.  When in doubt, backup [.filename]#/etc# and just accept "
"the merges."
msgstr "列出 `freebsd-update` 应尝试合并配置文件的目录。文件合并过程由一系列 man:diff[1] 补丁组成。合并操作可能会被接受、打开编辑器，或导致 `freebsd-update` 中止。如有疑问，请备份 [.filename]#/etc# 并直接接受合并结果。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:183
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Directory in which to store downloaded updates and temporary\n"
"# files used by FreeBSD Update.\n"
"# WorkDir /var/db/freebsd-update\n"
msgstr ""
"# Directory in which to store downloaded updates and temporary\n"
"# files used by FreeBSD Update.\n"
"# WorkDir /var/db/freebsd-update\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:187
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This directory is where all patches and temporary files are placed.  In "
"cases where the user is doing a version upgrade, this location should have "
"at least a gigabyte of disk space available."
msgstr ""
"这个目录是所有修补档和暂存盘的存放处。当使用者进行版本升级时，这个位置应该要"
"有至少1GB的可用磁盘空间。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:195
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# When upgrading between releases, should the list of Components be\n"
"# read strictly (StrictComponents yes) or merely as a list of components\n"
"# which *might* be installed of which FreeBSD Update should figure out\n"
"# which actually are installed and upgrade those (StrictComponents no)?\n"
"# StrictComponents no\n"
msgstr ""
"# When upgrading between releases, should the list of Components be\n"
"# read strictly (StrictComponents yes) or merely as a list of components\n"
"# which *might* be installed of which FreeBSD Update should figure out\n"
"# which actually are installed and upgrade those (StrictComponents no)?\n"
"# StrictComponents no\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:199
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When this option is set to `yes`, `freebsd-update` will assume that the "
"`Components` list is complete and will not attempt to make changes outside "
"of the list.  Effectively, `freebsd-update` will attempt to update every "
"file which belongs to the `Components` list."
msgstr "此选项设为 `yes` 时，`freebsd-update` 会假定 `Components` 列表是完整的，不会尝试更改列表之外的内容。实际上，`freebsd-update` 会尝试更新属于 `Components` 列表的每个文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:201
#, fuzzy
msgid "Refer to man:freebsd-update.conf[5] for more details."
msgstr "更多详情请参阅 man:freebsd-update.conf[5]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:203
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying Security Patches"
msgstr "套用安全性修补"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:207
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The process of applying FreeBSD security patches has been simplified, "
"allowing an administrator to keep a system fully patched using `freebsd-"
"update`.  More information about FreeBSD security advisories can be found in "
"crossref:security[security-advisories,\"FreeBSD Security Advisories\"]."
msgstr "应用 FreeBSD 安全补丁的过程已得到简化，管理员可以使用 `freebsd-update` 使系统保持完整修补状态。有关 FreeBSD 安全公告的更多信息，请参阅 crossref:security[security-advisories,\"FreeBSD 安全公告\"]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:211
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD security patches may be downloaded and installed using the following "
"commands.  The first command will determine if any outstanding patches are "
"available, and if so, will list the files that will be modified if the "
"patches are applied.  The second command will apply the patches."
msgstr ""
"FreeBSD安全性修补可以使用以下指令下载并安装。第一个指令会侦测是否有可用的修"
"补，如果有，将列出若执行修补后会变更的文件清单。第二个指令将会套用修补。"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:216
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:306
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# freebsd-update fetch\n"
"# freebsd-update install\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update fetch\n# freebsd-update install\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:220
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the update applies any kernel patches, the system will need a reboot in "
"order to boot into the patched kernel.  If the patch was applied to any "
"running binaries, the affected applications should be restarted so that the "
"patched version of the binary is used."
msgstr ""
"如果更新套用了任何核心修补，系统将会需要重启以使用修补过的核心。如果修补套用"
"在任何执行中的Binary，受影响的应用程序应重新启动来使用修补过的Binary版本。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:226
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Usually, the user needs to be prepared to reboot the system.  To know if the "
"system requires a reboot due to a kernel update, execute the commands "
"`freebsd-version -k` and `uname -r`.  Reboot the system if the outputs "
"differ."
msgstr ""
"通常情况下，用户需要准备重启系统。要知道内核更新是否需要重启，请执行"
"<command>freebsd-version -k</command>和<command>uname -r</command>命令，如果"
"输出不同，则需要重启。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:229
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The system can be configured to automatically check for updates once every "
"day by adding this entry to [.filename]#/etc/crontab#:"
msgstr ""
"加入以下项目至<filename>/etc/crontab</filename>可设定系统每天自动检查更新一"
"次："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:233
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "@daily                                  root    freebsd-update cron\n"
msgstr "@daily                                  root    freebsd-update cron\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:237
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If patches exist, they will automatically be downloaded but will not be "
"applied.  The `root` user will be sent an email so that the patches may be "
"reviewed and manually installed with `freebsd-update install`."
msgstr "如果存在补丁，系统会自动下载，但不会应用。系统会向 `root` 用户发送电子邮件，以便其审查补丁并使用 `freebsd-update install` 手动安装。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:239
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If anything goes wrong, `freebsd-update` has the ability to roll back the "
"last set of changes with the following command:"
msgstr ""
"如果有发生任何错误，<command>freebsd-update</command>可以使用以下指令还原最后"
"所做的变更："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:244
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# freebsd-update rollback\n"
"Uninstalling updates... done.\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update rollback\n正在卸载更新……完成。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:247
msgid ""
"Again, the system should be restarted if the kernel or any kernel modules "
"were modified and any affected binaries should be restarted."
msgstr ""
"再次强调，若核心或任何核心模块有做过修改应重新启动系统，以及任何受影响的"
"Binary应重新执行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:252
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Only the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel can be automatically updated by "
"`freebsd-update`.  If a custom kernel is installed, it will have to be "
"rebuilt and reinstalled after `freebsd-update` finishes installing the "
"updates.  The default kernel name is _GENERIC_.  The man:uname[1] command "
"may be used to verify its installation."
msgstr "`freebsd-update` 只能自动更新 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核。如果安装了自定义内核，则必须在 `freebsd-update` 完成更新安装后重新构建并安装该内核。默认内核名称为 _GENERIC_。可以使用 man:uname[1] 命令确认内核是否已安装。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:258
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Always keep a copy of the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel in [.filename]#/boot/"
"GENERIC#.  It will be helpful in diagnosing a variety of problems and in "
"performing version upgrades.  Refer to crossref:cutting-edge[freebsd-update-"
"custom-kernel-9x, Custom Kernels with FreeBSD 9.X and Later] for "
"instructions on how to get a copy of the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel."
msgstr "务必在 [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC# 中保留一份 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核副本。它有助于诊断各种问题和执行版本升级。有关如何获取 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核副本的说明，请参阅 crossref:cutting-edge[freebsd-update-custom-kernel-9x,FreeBSD 9.X 及更高版本中的自定义内核]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:263
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Unless the default configuration in [.filename]#/etc/freebsd-update.conf# "
"has been changed, `freebsd-update` will install the updated kernel sources "
"along with the rest of the updates.  Rebuilding and reinstalling a new "
"custom kernel can then be performed in the usual way."
msgstr ""
"除非在<filename>/etc/freebsd-update.conf</filename>的预设配置文件被修改，否则"
"<command>freebsd-update</command>将会安装更新后的核心源码和其余的更新，可依平"
"常的方式执行重新编译与重新安装核心。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:270
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The updates distributed by `freebsd-update` do not always involve the "
"kernel.  It is not necessary to rebuild a custom kernel if the kernel "
"sources have not been modified by `freebsd-update install`.  However, "
"`freebsd-update` will always update [.filename]#/usr/src/sys/conf/newvers."
"sh#.  The current patch level, as indicated by the `-p` number reported by "
"`uname -r`, is obtained from this file.  Rebuilding a custom kernel, even if "
"nothing else changed, allows `uname` to accurately report the current patch "
"level of the system.  This is particularly helpful when maintaining multiple "
"systems, as it allows for a quick assessment of the updates installed in "
"each one."
msgstr ""
"以<command>freebsd-update</command>发行的更新并非总是会更新核心。若核心的源码"
"没有被<command>freebsd-update install</command>修改则不需要重新编译自定义的核"
"心。虽然如此<command>freebsd-update</command>总是会更新<filename>/usr/src/"
"sys/conf/newvers.sh</filename>，目前修补的版本如<command>uname -r</command>执"
"行结果中的<literal>-p</literal>数字，便是由该档取得。即使没有做任何其他变更，"
"重新编译自定义核心可让<command>uname</command>准确的回报系统目前的修补版本。"
"当维护多个系统时这会特别有用，因其可让你快速评价每个系统安装的更新。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:272
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Performing Major and Minor Version Upgrades"
msgid "Performing Minor and Major Version Upgrades"
msgstr "执行主要及次要版号升级"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:275
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Upgrading to a newer minor or major version can be performed by providing "
"`freebsd-update` with a release version target."
msgstr "升级到较新的次要版本或主要版本时，可以向 `freebsd-update` 指定目标发行版本。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:281
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After each new `RELEASE`, FreeBSD package build servers will, for a limited "
"period, *not* use the newer version of the operating system.  This provides "
"continuity for the many users who do not upgrade immediately after a release "
"announcement.  For example:"
msgstr "每次发布新的 `RELEASE` 后，FreeBSD 软件包构建服务器会在有限时间内暂不使用较新版本的操作系统。这样可以照顾许多不会在发行公告发布后立即升级的用户。例如："

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:283
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"packages for users of 13.1 and 13.2 will be built on a server running 13.1, "
"until 13.1 reaches end of life"
msgstr "面向 13.1 和 13.2 用户的软件包会在运行 13.1 的服务器上构建，直至 13.1 停止支持"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:285
#, fuzzy
msgid "and, critically:"
msgstr "更重要的是："

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:287
#, fuzzy
msgid "a kernel module that is built on 13.1 might *not* be suitable for 13.2."
msgstr "在 13.1 上构建的内核模块可能不适用于 13.2。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:289
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So, with any minor or major OS upgrade, if the package requirements include "
"any kernel module:"
msgstr "因此，在进行任何次要版本或主要版本的操作系统升级时，如果软件包依赖项中包含内核模块："

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:291
#, fuzzy
msgid "*be prepared to build the module from source*."
msgstr "*请做好从源代码构建该模块的准备*。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:298
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the system is running a custom kernel, make sure that a copy of the [."
"filename]#GENERIC# kernel exists in [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC# before "
"starting the upgrade.  Refer to crossref:cutting-edge[freebsd-update-custom-"
"kernel-9x, Custom Kernels with FreeBSD 9.X and Later] for instructions on "
"how to get a copy of the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel."
msgstr "如果系统运行的是自定义内核，请在开始升级前确认 [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC# 中存在 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核副本。有关如何获取 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核副本的说明，请参阅 crossref:cutting-edge[freebsd-update-custom-kernel-9x,FreeBSD 9.X 及更高版本中的自定义内核]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:301
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before upgrading to a new version, ensure the existing FreeBSD installation "
"is up to date with respect to security and errata patches:"
msgstr "升级到新版本之前，请确保现有 FreeBSD 安装已应用最新的安全补丁和勘误补丁："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:309
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The following command, when run on a FreeBSD 9.0 system, will upgrade it "
#| "to FreeBSD 9.1:"
msgid ""
"The following command, when run on a FreeBSD 13.1 system, will upgrade it to "
"FreeBSD 13.2:"
msgstr "在FreeBSD 9.0系统执行以下指令，将会把系统升级至FreeBSD 9.1："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:313
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# freebsd-update -r 13.2-RELEASE upgrade\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update -r 13.2-RELEASE upgrade\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:318
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After the command has been received, `freebsd-update` will evaluate the "
"configuration file and current system in an attempt to gather the "
"information necessary to perform the upgrade.  A screen listing will display "
"which components have and have not been detected.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"收到这个指令后，<command>freebsd-update</command>会开始评价配置文件和目前的系"
"统来收集升级所需的信息。屏幕会显示侦测到或没侦测到的元件清单。例如："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:325
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Looking up update.FreeBSD.org mirrors... 1 mirrors found.\n"
"Fetching metadata signature for 13.1-RELEASE from update1.FreeBSD.org... done.\n"
"Fetching metadata index... done.\n"
"Inspecting system... done.\n"
msgstr "正在查找 update.FreeBSD.org 镜像……找到 1 个镜像。\n正在从 update1.FreeBSD.org 获取 13.1-RELEASE 的元数据签名……完成。\n正在获取元数据索引……完成。\n正在检查系统……完成。\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:331
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following components of FreeBSD seem to be installed:\n"
"kernel/smp src/base src/bin src/contrib src/crypto src/etc src/games\n"
"src/gnu src/include src/krb5 src/lib src/libexec src/release src/rescue\n"
"src/sbin src/secure src/share src/sys src/tools src/ubin src/usbin\n"
"world/base world/info world/lib32 world/manpages\n"
msgstr "以下 FreeBSD 组件似乎已安装：\nkernel/smp src/base src/bin src/contrib src/crypto src/etc src/games\nsrc/gnu src/include src/krb5 src/lib src/libexec src/release src/rescue\nsrc/sbin src/secure src/share src/sys src/tools src/ubin src/usbin\nworld/base world/info world/lib32 world/manpages\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:335
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following components of FreeBSD do not seem to be installed:\n"
"kernel/generic world/catpages world/dict world/doc world/games\n"
"world/proflibs\n"
msgstr "以下 FreeBSD 组件似乎未安装：\nkernel/generic world/catpages world/dict world/doc world/games\nworld/proflibs\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:337
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Does this look reasonable (y/n)? y\n"
msgstr "这样看起来合理吗（y/n）？ y\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:341
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"At this point, `freebsd-update` will attempt to download all files required "
"for the upgrade.  In some cases, the user may be prompted with questions "
"regarding what to install or how to proceed."
msgstr ""
"此时，<command>freebsd-update</command>将会尝试下载所有升级需要的文件。在某些"
"情况，会询问使用者一些关于要安装什么或要如何继续。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:343
msgid ""
"When using a custom kernel, the above step will produce a warning similar to "
"the following:"
msgstr "当使用自定义核心，上述的步骤将会产生如下的警告："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:350
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"WARNING: This system is running a \"MYKERNEL\" kernel, which is not a\n"
"kernel configuration distributed as part of FreeBSD 13.1-RELEASE.\n"
"This kernel will not be updated: you MUST update the kernel manually\n"
"before running \"/usr/sbin/freebsd-update install\"\n"
msgstr "警告：此系统运行的是“MYKERNEL”内核，该内核配置并非 FreeBSD 13.1-RELEASE 的发行内容。\n此内核不会更新：运行“/usr/sbin/freebsd-update install”之前，必须手动更新内核\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:354
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This warning may be safely ignored at this point.  The updated [."
"filename]#GENERIC# kernel will be used as an intermediate step in the "
"upgrade process."
msgstr ""
"这时的警告可以安全地忽略，升级过程将会使用更新过的<filename>GENERIC</"
"filename>核心来进行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:363
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once all the patches have been downloaded to the local system, they will be "
"applied.  This process may take a while, depending on the speed and workload "
"of the machine.  Configuration files will then be merged.  The merging "
"process requires some user intervention as a file may be merged or an editor "
"may appear on screen for a manual merge.  The results of every successful "
"merge will be shown to the user as the process continues.  A failed or "
"ignored merge will cause the process to abort.  Users may wish to make a "
"backup of [.filename]#/etc# and manually merge important files, such as [."
"filename]#master.passwd# or [.filename]#group# at a later time."
msgstr ""
"所有的修补都下载到本地系统之后，将会开始套用更新。这个过程可能会花点时间，取"
"决于机器的速度和工作量。配置文件将会被合并。合并的过程中当文件被合并或是手动"
"合并画面上出现编辑器时需要使用者操作。每一个成功合并的结果将会显示给使用者并"
"继续程序，失败或忽略合并将会使程序中断。使用者可能想要备份<filename>/etc</"
"filename>并稍后手动合并重要的文件，例如：<filename>master.passwd</filename>或"
"<filename>group</filename>。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:370
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The system is not being altered yet as all patching and merging is happening "
"in another directory.  Once all patches have been applied successfully, all "
"configuration files have been merged and it seems the process will go "
"smoothly, the changes can be committed to disk by the user using the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""
"所有的修补与合并动作会在另一个目录进行，并不会直接修改。当成功套用所有修补，"
"所有配置文件已合并且过程顺利，使用者可使用以下指令将变更安装到磁盘："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:374
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:410
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:487
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# freebsd-update install\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update install\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:381
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The kernel and kernel modules will be patched first.  If the system is "
"running with a custom kernel, use man:nextboot[8] to set the kernel for the "
"next boot to the updated [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC#:"
msgstr "首先会修补内核和内核模块。如果系统运行的是自定义内核，请使用 man:nextboot[8] 将下次启动的内核设置为已更新的 [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC#："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:385
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# nextboot -k GENERIC\n"
msgstr "# nextboot -k GENERIC\n"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:394
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before rebooting with the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel, make sure it contains "
"all the drivers required for the system to boot properly and connect to the "
"network, if the machine being updated is accessed remotely.  In particular, "
"if the running custom kernel contains built-in functionality usually "
"provided by kernel modules, make sure to temporarily load these modules into "
"the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel using the [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# "
"facility.  It is recommended to disable non-essential services as well as "
"any disk and network mounts until the upgrade process is complete."
msgstr ""
"若机器在远端进行更新，请在使用<filename>GENERIC</filename>核心重启前，请确定"
"该核心含有所有系统所需的驱动程序以正常开机并联机至网络。特别是在执行的自定义"
"核心有使用到由核心模块提供内置功能，请确定将这些模块已暂时使用<filename>/"
"boot/loader.conf</filename>配置文件加载到<filename>GENERIC</filename>核心。建"
"议关闭非必须的服务和磁盘与网络挂载直到升级程序完成。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:397
msgid "The machine should now be restarted with the updated kernel:"
msgstr "机器现在应使用更新过的核心重启："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:401
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1104
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1251
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# shutdown -r now\n"
msgstr "# shutdown -r now\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:406
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once the system has come back online, restart `freebsd-update` using the "
"following command.  Since the state of the process has been saved, `freebsd-"
"update` will not start from the beginning, but will instead move on to the "
"next phase and remove all old shared libraries and object files."
msgstr ""
"一旦系统重新上线，使用以下指令继续<command>freebsd-update</command>。由于程序"
"的状态已被储存，<command>freebsd-update</command>不会重头开始，但会进行下一个"
"阶段并移除所有旧的共享程序库和目标档。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:415
msgid ""
"Depending upon whether any library version numbers were bumped, there may "
"only be two install phases instead of three."
msgstr "取决于是否有任何程序库版本编号冲突，也可能只有两个而不是三个安装阶段。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:420
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The upgrade is now complete.  If this was a major version upgrade, reinstall "
"all ports and packages as described in crossref:cutting-edge[freebsdupdate-"
"portsrebuild, Upgrading Packages After a Major Version Upgrade]."
msgstr "升级现已完成。如果这是一次主要版本升级，请按照 crossref:cutting-edge[freebsdupdate-portsrebuild,主要版本升级后升级软件包] 中的说明重新安装所有 ports 和软件包。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:422
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom Kernels with FreeBSD 9.X and Later"
msgstr "在FreeBSD 9.X及之后版本自定义核心"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:427
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before using `freebsd-update`, ensure that a copy of the [."
"filename]#GENERIC# kernel exists in [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC#.  If a custom "
"kernel has only been built once, the kernel in [.filename]#/boot/kernel.old# "
"is the `GENERIC` kernel.  Simply rename this directory to [.filename]#/boot/"
"GENERIC#."
msgstr "使用 `freebsd-update` 之前，请确保 [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC# 中存在 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核副本。如果自定义内核只构建过一次，那么 [.filename]#/boot/kernel.old# 中的内核就是 `GENERIC` 内核。只需将此目录重命名为 [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC#。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:431
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If a custom kernel has been built more than once or if it is unknown how "
"many times the custom kernel has been built, obtain a copy of the `GENERIC` "
"kernel that matches the current version of the operating system.  If "
"physical access to the system is available, a copy of the `GENERIC` kernel "
"can be installed from the installation media:"
msgstr ""
"若有编译自定义核心过超过一次，或已经不晓得编译自定义核心的次数，则需取得与目"
"前操作系统版本相符的<literal>GENERIC</literal>核心复本。若可直接操作实体系"
"统，则可以从安装媒体取得<literal> GENERIC</literal>核心复本："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:437
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# mount /media\n"
"# cd /media/usr/freebsd-dist\n"
"# tar -C/ -xvf kernel.txz boot/kernel/kernel\n"
msgstr "# mount /media\n# cd /media/usr/freebsd-dist\n# tar -C/ -xvf kernel.txz boot/kernel/kernel\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:440
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Alternately, the `GENERIC` kernel may be rebuilt and installed from source:"
msgstr "也可以从源代码重新构建并安装 `GENERIC` 内核："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:445
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/src\n"
"# make kernel __MAKE_CONF=/dev/null SRCCONF=/dev/null\n"
msgstr "# cd /usr/src\n# make kernel __MAKE_CONF=/dev/null SRCCONF=/dev/null\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:450
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For this kernel to be identified as the `GENERIC` kernel by `freebsd-"
"update`, the [.filename]#GENERIC# configuration file must not have been "
"modified in any way.  It is also suggested that the kernel is built without "
"any other special options."
msgstr "要让 `freebsd-update` 将此内核识别为 `GENERIC` 内核，必须确保 [.filename]#GENERIC# 配置文件未经过任何修改。此外，建议构建内核时不要使用其他特殊选项。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:452
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Rebooting into the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel is not required as `freebsd-"
"update` only needs [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC# to exist."
msgstr "无需重新启动进入 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核，因为 `freebsd-update` 只要求 [.filename]#/boot/GENERIC# 存在。"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:454
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upgrading Packages After a Major Version Upgrade"
msgstr "主要版号升级后的套件升级"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:461
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Generally, installed applications will continue to work without problems "
"after minor version upgrades.  Major versions use different Application "
"Binary Interfaces (ABIs), which will break most third-party applications.  "
"After a major version upgrade, all installed packages and ports need to be "
"upgraded.  Packages can be upgraded using `pkg upgrade`.  To upgrade "
"installed ports, use a utility such as package:ports-mgmt/portmaster[]."
msgstr "通常，已安装的应用程序在次要版本升级后仍可正常运行。主要版本使用不同的应用程序二进制接口（ABI），这会导致大多数第三方应用程序无法运行。主要版本升级后，必须升级所有已安装的软件包和 ports。可以使用 `pkg upgrade` 升级软件包。要升级已安装的 ports，可使用 package:ports-mgmt/portmaster[] 等工具。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:465
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A forced upgrade of all installed packages will replace the packages with "
"fresh versions from the repository even if the version number has not "
"increased.  This is required because of the ABI version change when "
"upgrading between major versions of FreeBSD.  The forced upgrade can be "
"accomplished by performing:"
msgstr ""
"强制升级所有已安装的套件会使用文件库中新版本的套件来取得目前套件，即使该版号"
"没有增加。由于在升级FreeBSD主要版本时会变更ABI版本，因此这是必要动作。强制升"
"级可以执行以下指令来完成："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:469
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# pkg-static upgrade -f\n"
msgstr "# pkg-static upgrade -f\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:472
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "A rebuild of all installed applications can be accomplished with this "
#| "command:"
msgid ""
"A rebuild of all applications installed from the ports collection can be "
"accomplished with this command:"
msgstr "重新编译所有已安装的应用程序可以执行以下指令来完成："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:476
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# portmaster -af\n"
msgstr "# portmaster -af\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:480
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This command will display the configuration screens for each application "
"that has configurable options and wait for the user to interact with those "
"screens.  To prevent this behavior, and use only the default options, "
"include `-G` in the above command."
msgstr ""
"这个指令会在安装每个应用程序有可设定选项时显示设定画面，并会等待使用者操作该"
"画面，要避免这种情况并使用预设的设定选项，可在上述指令加上<option>-G</option>"
"参数。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:483
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once the software upgrades are complete, finish the upgrade process with a "
"final call to `freebsd-update` in order to tie up all the loose ends in the "
"upgrade process:"
msgstr ""
"完成软件升级后，最后需执行<command>freebsd-update</command>来完成最后的升级动"
"作："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:491
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the [.filename]#GENERIC# kernel was temporarily used, this is the time to "
"build and install a new custom kernel using the instructions in crossref:"
"kernelconfig[kernelconfig,Configuring the FreeBSD Kernel]."
msgstr "如果之前临时使用了 [.filename]#GENERIC# 内核，现在就应按照 crossref:kernelconfig[kernelconfig,配置 FreeBSD 内核] 中的说明构建并安装新的自定义内核。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:494
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Reboot the machine into the new FreeBSD version.  The upgrade process is now "
"complete."
msgstr "重启使用新的FreeBSD版本后，升级程序便正式完成。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:496
#, no-wrap
msgid "System State Comparison"
msgstr "比对系统状态"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:500
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The state of the installed FreeBSD version against a known good copy can be "
"tested using `freebsd-update IDS`.  This command evaluates the current "
"version of system utilities, libraries, and configuration files and can be "
"used as a built-in Intrusion Detection System (IDS)."
msgstr ""
"已安装的FreeBSD版本状态可以使用<command>freebsd-update IDS</command>与另一个"
"已知良好的复本来做比对测试。这个指令会评价目前版本的系统工具，程序库和配置文"
"件，可做为内置的入侵侦测系统来使用（Intrusion Detection System，"
"<acronym>IDS</acronym>）。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:508
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This command is not a replacement for a real IDS such as package:security/"
"snort[].  As `freebsd-update` stores data on disk, the possibility of "
"tampering is evident.  While this possibility may be reduced using `kern."
"securelevel` and by storing the `freebsd-update` data on a read-only file "
"system when not in use, a better solution would be to compare the system "
"against a secure disk, such as a DVD or securely stored external USB disk "
"device.  An alternative method for providing IDS functionality using a built-"
"in utility is described in crossref:security[security-ids,\"Binary "
"Verification\"]"
msgstr "此命令不能替代 package:security/snort[] 等真正的 IDS。由于 `freebsd-update` 会在磁盘上存储数据，因此存在数据遭篡改的可能。使用 `kern.securelevel` 并在不使用时将 `freebsd-update` 数据存储在只读文件系统上，可以降低这种风险；更好的解决方案是将系统与安全磁盘（例如 DVD 或妥善保管的外置 USB 磁盘设备）进行比较。关于使用内置工具实现 IDS 功能的替代方法，请参阅 crossref:security[security-ids,\"二进制验证\"]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:511
msgid ""
"To begin the comparison, specify the output file to save the results to:"
msgstr "要开始比对，需指定输出的文件来储存结果："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:515
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# freebsd-update IDS >> outfile.ids\n"
msgstr "# freebsd-update IDS >> outfile.ids\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:518
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The system will now be inspected and a lengthy listing of files, along with "
"the SHA256 hash values for both the known value in the release and the "
"current installation, will be sent to the specified output file."
msgstr ""
"系统将会开始检查并且会产生相当长的文件清单，内容包含发布版本已知的与目前安装"
"版本的<acronym>SHA256</acronym>哈希值会储存到指定的输出档。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:521
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The entries in the listing are extremely long, but the output format may be "
"easily parsed.  For instance, to obtain a list of all files which differ "
"from those in the release, issue the following command:"
msgstr ""
"清单中的项目会相当的多，但输出的格式可以很简单的用来分析。例如，要取得与发布"
"版本不同的文件清单，可使用以下指令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:529
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cat outfile.ids | awk '{ print $1 }' | more\n"
"/etc/master.passwd\n"
"/etc/motd\n"
"/etc/passwd\n"
"/etc/pf.conf\n"
msgstr "# cat outfile.ids | awk '{ print $1 }' | more\n/etc/master.passwd\n/etc/motd\n/etc/passwd\n/etc/pf.conf\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:536
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This sample output has been truncated as many more files exist.  Some files "
"have natural modifications.  For example, [.filename]#/etc/passwd# will be "
"modified if users have been added to the system.  Kernel modules may differ "
"as `freebsd-update` may have updated them.  To exclude specific files or "
"directories, add them to the `IDSIgnorePaths` option in [.filename]#/etc/"
"freebsd-update.conf#."
msgstr ""
"实际的文件会更多，此示例的输出已精简。部份文件可能本来就会被修改。例如"
"<filename>/etc/passwd</filename>在新增使用者到系统时会被修改，核心模块也有可"
"能因使用<command>freebsd-update</command>更新而有所不同。要排除特定的文件或目"
"录可将这些文件或目录加入到<filename>/etc/freebsd-update.conf</filename>中的"
"<literal>IDSIgnorePaths</literal>选项。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:538
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Updating the Source"
msgid "Updating Bootcode"
msgstr "更新源码"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:541
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The following manuals describe the upgrade process of bootcode and boot "
"loaders: man:gpart[8], man:gptboot[8], man:gptzfsboot[8], and man:loader."
"efi[8]."
msgstr "以下手册介绍了引导代码和引导加载程序的升级过程：man:gpart[8]、man:gptboot[8]、man:gptzfsboot[8] 和 man:loader.efi[8]。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:543
#, no-wrap
msgid "Updating the Documentation Set"
msgstr "更新文件集"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:547
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Documentation is an integral part of the FreeBSD operating system.  While an "
"up-to-date version of the FreeBSD documentation is always available on the "
"FreeBSD web site (link:https://docs.FreeBSD.org[Documentation Portal]), it "
"can be handy to have an up-to-date, local copy of the FreeBSD website, "
"handbooks, FAQ, and articles."
msgstr "文档是 FreeBSD 操作系统不可或缺的一部分。虽然 FreeBSD 网站上始终提供最新版本的 FreeBSD 文档（link:https://docs.FreeBSD.org[文档门户]），但拥有一份本地最新副本也很方便，其中包括 FreeBSD 网站、手册、常见问题解答和文章。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:549
msgid ""
"This section describes how to use either source or the FreeBSD Ports "
"Collection to keep a local copy of the FreeBSD documentation up-to-date."
msgstr ""
"本节将说明如何使用源码与FreeBSD Port套件集来取得最新版本FreeBSD文件本地复本。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:552
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For information on editing and submitting corrections to the documentation, "
"refer to the FreeBSD Documentation Project Primer for New Contributors "
"(extref:{fdp-primer}[FreeBSD Documentation Project Primer for New "
"Contributors])."
msgstr "有关如何编辑文档以及提交更正的信息，请参阅《FreeBSD 文档项目新贡献者入门指南》（extref:{fdp-primer}[FreeBSD 文档项目新贡献者入门指南]）。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:554
#, no-wrap
msgid "Updating Documentation from Source"
msgstr "自源码更新说明文件"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:558
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Rebuilding the FreeBSD documentation from source requires a collection of "
"tools which are not part of the FreeBSD base system.  The required tools can "
"be installed following extref:{fdp-primer}overview[these steps, overview-"
"quick-start] from the FreeBSD Documentation Project Primer."
msgstr "从源代码重新构建 FreeBSD 文档需要一组不属于 FreeBSD 基本系统的工具。可以按照《FreeBSD 文档项目新贡献者入门指南》中的 extref:{fdp-primer}overview[这些步骤，快速入门概述] 安装所需工具。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:560
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once installed, use `git` to fetch a clean copy of the documentation source:"
msgstr "安装完成后，使用 `git` 获取一份干净的文档源代码副本："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:564
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# git clone https://git.FreeBSD.org/doc.git /usr/doc\n"
msgstr "# git clone https://git.FreeBSD.org/doc.git /usr/doc\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:568
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The initial download of the documentation sources may take a while.  Let it "
"run until it completes."
msgstr "第一次下载文件源码需要一些时间，请耐心等候执行完毕。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:570
msgid "Future updates of the documentation sources may be fetched by running:"
msgstr "往后更新文件源码可执行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:574
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# git pull\n"
msgstr "# git pull\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:578
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once an up-to-date snapshot of the documentation sources has been fetched to "
"[.filename]#/usr/doc#, everything is ready for an update of the installed "
"documentation."
msgstr ""
"下载最新的文件源码到<filename>/usr/doc</filename>之后，便完成要更新已安装文件"
"的准备动作。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:580
#, fuzzy
msgid "A full update may be performed by typing:"
msgstr "可以通过输入以下命令执行完整更新："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:585
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/doc\n"
"# make\n"
msgstr "# cd /usr/doc\n# make\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:588
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tracking a Development Branch"
msgstr "追踪开发分支"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:591
msgid ""
"FreeBSD has two development branches: FreeBSD-CURRENT and FreeBSD-STABLE."
msgstr "FreeBSD有两个开发分支：FreeBSD-CURRENT及FreeBSD-STABLE。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:593
msgid ""
"This section provides an explanation of each branch and its intended "
"audience, as well as how to keep a system up-to-date with each respective "
"branch."
msgstr ""
"本节将说明每个分支及其的特定使用者，也会说明如何在各别分支维持系统为最新版。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:595
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using FreeBSD-CURRENT"
msgstr "使用FreeBSD-CURRENT"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:599
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD-CURRENT is the \"bleeding edge\" of FreeBSD development and FreeBSD-"
"CURRENT users are expected to have a high degree of technical skill.  Less "
"technical users who wish to track a development branch should track FreeBSD-"
"STABLE instead."
msgstr ""
"FreeBSD-CURRENT是FreeBSD开发的<quote>最前线</quote>，FreeBSD-CURRENT的使用者"
"需具备较强的技术能力。技术能力较弱的使用者应改追踪FreeBSD-STABLE开发分支。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:603
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD-CURRENT is the very latest source code for FreeBSD and includes "
"works in progress, experimental changes, and transitional mechanisms that "
"might or might not be present in the next official release.  While many "
"FreeBSD developers compile the FreeBSD-CURRENT source code daily, there are "
"short periods of time when the source may not be buildable.  These problems "
"are resolved as quickly as possible, but whether or not FreeBSD-CURRENT "
"brings disaster or new functionality can be a matter of when the source code "
"was synced."
msgstr ""
"FreeBSD-CURRENT是FreeBSD最新的源码，其中包括正在进行的开发工作、实验性的变更"
"以及不一定会在下一个官方发行版出现的过渡机制。虽然FreeBSD开发者每天编译"
"FreeBSD-CURRENT源码，但仍可能有短暂时间源码是无法编译的。虽然这些问题会尽快被"
"解决，但是无论FreeBSD-CURRENT带来灾难或是新功能，同步源码时都要考察这个问题。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:605
msgid "FreeBSD-CURRENT is made available for three primary interest groups:"
msgstr "FreeBSD-CURRENT主要给下以三种族群："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:607
msgid ""
"Members of the FreeBSD community who are actively working on some part of "
"the source tree."
msgstr "致力于开发某一部份源码树的FreeBSD社群成员。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:608
msgid ""
"Members of the FreeBSD community who are active testers. They are willing to "
"spend time solving problems, making topical suggestions on changes and the "
"general direction of FreeBSD, and submitting patches."
msgstr ""
"FreeBSD社群成员中活耀的测试人员。他们愿意花时间解决问题，对FreeBSD的变更及大"
"方向提出专业建议并送交修补。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:609
msgid ""
"Users who wish to keep an eye on things, use the current source for "
"reference purposes, or make the occasional comment or code contribution."
msgstr ""
"随时关注的使用者，使用目前源码做为参考用途，或是偶尔提供意见或贡献源码。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:613
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD-CURRENT should _not_ be considered a fast-track to getting new "
"features before the next release as pre-release features are not yet fully "
"tested and most likely contain bugs.  It is not a quick way of getting bug "
"fixes as any given commit is just as likely to introduce new bugs as to fix "
"existing ones.  FreeBSD-CURRENT is not in any way \"officially supported\"."
msgstr "FreeBSD-CURRENT __不应__被视为在下一个版本发布前获取新功能的捷径，因为预发布功能尚未经过充分测试，而且很可能包含错误。它也不是快速获取错误修复的方式，因为任何给定的提交都同样可能引入新错误或修复现有错误。FreeBSD-CURRENT 并非任何意义上的“官方支持”版本。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:615
msgid "To track FreeBSD-CURRENT:"
msgstr "若要追踪FreeBSD-CURRENT："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:617
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Join the {freebsd-current} and the {dev-commits-src-main} lists. This is "
"_essential_ in order to see the comments that people are making about the "
"current state of the system and to receive important bulletins about the "
"current state of FreeBSD-CURRENT."
msgstr "加入 {freebsd-current} 和 {dev-commits-src-main} 邮件列表。要了解人们对系统当前状态的评论，并接收有关 FreeBSD-CURRENT 当前状态的重要公告，这__至关重要__。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:619
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The {dev-commits-src-main} list records the commit log entry for each change "
"as it is made, along with any pertinent information on possible side effects."
msgstr "{dev-commits-src-main} 邮件列表会记录每项更改的提交日志条目，以及有关潜在副作用的任何相关信息。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:622
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To join these lists, go to {mailing-lists}, click on the list to subscribe "
"to, and follow the instructions.  In order to track changes to the whole "
"source tree, not just the changes to FreeBSD-CURRENT, subscribe to the {dev-"
"commits-src-all}."
msgstr "要加入这些邮件列表，请访问 {mailing-lists}，点击要订阅的列表，然后按照说明操作。要跟踪整个源代码树的更改，而不仅仅是 FreeBSD-CURRENT 的更改，请订阅 {dev-commits-src-all}。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:623
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Synchronize with the FreeBSD-CURRENT sources. Typically, `git` is used to "
"check out the -CURRENT code from the `main` branch of the FreeBSD Git "
"repository (see crossref:mirrors[git,“Using Git”] for details)."
msgstr "与 FreeBSD-CURRENT 源代码同步。通常使用 `git` 从 FreeBSD Git 仓库的 `main` 分支检出 -CURRENT 代码（详情请参见 crossref:mirrors[git,“使用 Git”]）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:624
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Due to the size of the repository, some users choose to only synchronize the "
"sections of source that interest them or which they are contributing patches "
"to. However, users that plan to compile the operating system from source "
"must download _all_ of FreeBSD-CURRENT, not just selected portions."
msgstr ""
"考察到文件库的大小，部份使用者选择只同步他们有兴趣或贡献修补的部份源码。然"
"而，计划要从源码编译整个操作系统的使用者须下载<emphasis>全部</emphasis>的"
"FreeBSD-CURRENT，不可只有选择的部份。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:628
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before compiling FreeBSD-CURRENT, read [.filename]#/usr/src/Makefile# very "
"carefully and follow the instructions in crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld, "
"Updating FreeBSD from Source].  Read the {freebsd-current} and [.filename]#/"
"usr/src/UPDATING# to stay up-to-date on other bootstrapping procedures that "
"sometimes become necessary on the road to the next release."
msgstr "在编译 FreeBSD-CURRENT 之前，请仔细阅读 [.filename]#/usr/src/Makefile#，并遵循 crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld, 从源代码更新 FreeBSD] 中的说明。请阅读 {freebsd-current} 和 [.filename]#/usr/src/UPDATING#，以了解在迈向下一个版本的过程中有时需要执行的其他引导程序步骤的最新信息。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:629
msgid ""
"Be active! FreeBSD-CURRENT users are encouraged to submit their suggestions "
"for enhancements or bug fixes. Suggestions with accompanying code are always "
"welcome."
msgstr ""
"积极点！建议 FreeBSD-CURRENT 用户提交增强功能或错误修复建议。始终欢迎附带代码"
"的建议。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:631
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using FreeBSD-STABLE"
msgstr "使用FreeBSD-CURRENT"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:638
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD-STABLE is the development branch from which major releases are "
"made.  Changes go into this branch at a slower pace and with the general "
"assumption that they have first been tested in FreeBSD-CURRENT.  This is "
"_still_ a development branch and, at any given time, the sources for FreeBSD-"
"STABLE may or may not be suitable for general use.  It is simply another "
"engineering development track, not a resource for end-users.  Users who do "
"not have the resources to perform testing should instead run the most recent "
"release of FreeBSD."
msgstr ""
"FreeBSD-STABLE 是我们的发展分支，我们的主要发行版就由此而来。 这个分支会以不"
"同速度变化，并且假定这些是第一次进入 FreeBSD-CURRENT 进行测试。然而，这 "
"<emphasis>仍然</emphasis> 是个发展中的分支，这意味着在一定的时候，FreeBSD-"
"STABLE 源码可能或不可能满足一些特殊的要求。 它只不过是另一个工程发展途径，并"
"不是终端用户的资源。没有执行测试的资源的用户应改为运行最新版本的 FreeBSD。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:640
msgid ""
"Those interested in tracking or contributing to the FreeBSD development "
"process, especially as it relates to the next release of FreeBSD, should "
"consider following FreeBSD-STABLE."
msgstr ""
"如果您有兴趣追随 FreeBSD 的开发过程或为其做点贡献， 尤其是和下一个非计划的 "
"FreeBSD 发行版有关时， 您应该考虑采用 FreeBSD-STABLE。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:645
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"While the FreeBSD-STABLE branch should compile and run at all times, this "
"cannot be guaranteed.  Since more people run FreeBSD-STABLE than FreeBSD-"
"CURRENT, it is inevitable that bugs and corner cases will sometimes be found "
"in FreeBSD-STABLE that were not apparent in FreeBSD-CURRENT.  For this "
"reason, one should not blindly track FreeBSD-STABLE.  It is particularly "
"important _not_ to update any production servers to FreeBSD-STABLE without "
"thoroughly testing the code in a development or testing environment."
msgstr ""
"尽管我们尽力确保 FreeBSD-STABLE 分支在任何时候都能够正确编译和运行， 但没有人"
"能够担保它在任何时候都总可以。此外，尽管代码在进入 FreeBSD-STABLE 之前都是在 "
"FreeBSD-CURRENT 上完成开发，但使用 FreeBSD-STABLE 的人要比使用 FreeBSD-"
"CURRENT 的更多。有证据显示， 犄角旮旯里的各种问题有些时候仍然会由于在 "
"FreeBSD-CURRENT 不那么明显 而在 FreeBSD-STABLE 暴露出来。基于这些原因， "
"<emphasis>不</emphasis> 推荐您盲目地追随 FreeBSD-STABLE， 并且， 在粗略地测试"
"过代码之前不要更新任何生产服务器到 FreeBSD-STABLE 也非常重要。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:647
msgid "To track FreeBSD-STABLE:"
msgstr "若要追踪FreeBSD-CURRENT："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:649
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Join the {freebsd-stable} in order to stay informed of build dependencies "
"that may appear in FreeBSD-STABLE or any other issues requiring special "
"attention. Developers will also make announcements in this mailing list when "
"they are contemplating some controversial fix or update, giving the users a "
"chance to respond if they have any issues to raise concerning the proposed "
"change."
msgstr "加入 {freebsd-stable}，以了解 FreeBSD-STABLE 中可能出现的构建依赖项或任何其他需要特别注意的问题。开发人员在考虑有争议的修复或更新时，也会在此邮件列表中发布公告，让用户有机会对拟议的更改提出意见。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:653
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Join the relevant git list for the branch being tracked.  For example, users "
"tracking the {betarel-current-major}-STABLE branch should join the {dev-"
"commits-src-branches}.  This list records the commit log entry for each "
"change as it is made, along with any pertinent information on possible side "
"effects."
msgstr "加入与所跟踪分支相关的 Git 邮件列表。例如，跟踪 {betarel-current-major}-STABLE 分支的用户应加入 {dev-commits-src-branches}。此列表会记录每项更改的提交日志条目，以及有关潜在副作用的任何相关信息。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:656
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To join these lists, go to {mailing-lists}, click on the list to subscribe "
"to, and follow the instructions.  In order to track changes for the whole "
"source tree, subscribe to {dev-commits-src-all}."
msgstr "要加入这些邮件列表，请访问 {mailing-lists}，点击要订阅的列表，然后按照说明操作。要跟踪整个源代码树的更改，请订阅 {dev-commits-src-all}。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:657
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To install a new FreeBSD-STABLE system, install the most recent FreeBSD-"
"STABLE release from the crossref:mirrors[mirrors,FreeBSD mirror sites] or "
"use a monthly snapshot built from FreeBSD-STABLE. Refer to link:https://www."
"FreeBSD.org/snapshots/[www.freebsd.org/snapshots] for more information about "
"snapshots."
msgstr "要安装新的 FreeBSD-STABLE 系统，请从 crossref:mirrors[mirrors,FreeBSD 镜像站点] 安装最新的 FreeBSD-STABLE 版本，或使用基于 FreeBSD-STABLE 构建的每月快照。有关快照的更多信息，请参阅 link:https://www.FreeBSD.org/snapshots/[www.freebsd.org/snapshots]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:660
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To compile or upgrade an existing FreeBSD system to FreeBSD-STABLE, use "
"`git` to check out the source for the desired branch.  Branch names, such as "
"`stable/13`, are listed at link:https://www.FreeBSD.org/releng/[www.freebsd."
"org/releng]."
msgstr "要将现有 FreeBSD 系统编译或升级到 FreeBSD-STABLE，请使用 `git` 检出所需分支的源代码。分支名称（例如 `stable/13`）列于 link:https://www.FreeBSD.org/releng/[www.freebsd.org/releng]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:663
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Before compiling or upgrading to FreeBSD-STABLE , read [.filename]#/usr/src/"
"Makefile# carefully and follow the instructions in crossref:cutting-"
"edge[makeworld, Updating FreeBSD from Source]. Read the {freebsd-stable} and "
"[.filename]#/usr/src/UPDATING# to keep up-to-date on other bootstrapping "
"procedures that sometimes become necessary on the road to the next release."
msgstr "在编译或升级到 FreeBSD-STABLE 之前，请仔细阅读 [.filename]#/usr/src/Makefile#，并遵循 crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld, 从源代码更新 FreeBSD] 中的说明。请阅读 {freebsd-stable} 和 [.filename]#/usr/src/UPDATING#，以了解在迈向下一个版本的过程中有时需要执行的其他引导程序步骤的最新信息。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:665
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "The N-number"
msgstr "N 编号"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:669
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When tracking down bugs it is important to know which versions of the source "
"code have been used to create the system exhibiting an issue.  FreeBSD "
"provides version information compiled into the kernel.  man:uname[1] "
"retrieves this information, for example:"
msgstr "排查错误时，了解用于构建出现问题的系统的源代码版本非常重要。FreeBSD 会将版本信息编译进内核。可以使用 man:uname[1] 获取这些信息，例如："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:673
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% uname -v\n"
"FreeBSD 14.0-CURRENT #112 main-n247514-031260d64c18: Tue Jun 22 20:43:19 MDT 2021     fred@machine:/usr/home/fred/obj/usr/home/fred/git/head/amd64.amd64/sys/FRED\n"
msgstr "% uname -v\nFreeBSD 14.0-CURRENT #112 main-n247514-031260d64c18: Tue Jun 22 20:43:19 MDT 2021     fred@machine:/usr/home/fred/obj/usr/home/fred/git/head/amd64.amd64/sys/FRED\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:676
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The final field gives information regarding the kernel name, the person that "
"built it, and the location that it was compiled in.  Looking at the 4th "
"field, it is made up of several parts:"
msgstr "最后一个字段提供内核名称、构建者以及编译位置的信息。第 4 个字段由几个部分组成："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:679
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "main-n247514-031260d64c18\n"
msgstr "main-n247514-031260d64c18\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:684
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"main\t\t<.>\n"
"n247514\t\t<.>\n"
"031260d64c18\t<.>\n"
"\t\t<.>\n"
msgstr "main\t\t<.>\nn247514\t\t<.>\n031260d64c18\t<.>\n\t\t<.>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:688
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Git branch name.  Note: comparisons of n-numbers are only valid on branches "
"published by the project (`main`, `stable/XX` and `releng/XX`).  Local "
"branches will have n-numbers that will overlap commits of their parent "
"branch."
msgstr "Git 分支名称。注意：只有在项目发布的分支（`main`、`stable/XX` 和 `releng/XX`）上，N 编号之间的比较才有效。本地分支的 N 编号可能与其父分支中的提交编号重叠。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:689
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The n-number is a linear count of commits back to the start of the Git "
"repository starting with the Git hash included in the line."
msgstr "N 编号是从 Git 仓库起始处到当前提交的线性提交计数，起始点为该行中包含的 Git 哈希值。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:690
#, fuzzy
msgid "Git hash of the checked out tree"
msgstr "已检出树的 Git 哈希值"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:692
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Sometimes a suffix of `-dirty` is present when the kernel was built in a "
"tree with uncommitted changes.  It is absent in this example because the "
"FRED kernel was built from a pristine checkout."
msgstr "如果内核是在包含未提交更改的代码树中构建的，有时会带有 `-dirty` 后缀。本例中没有该后缀，因为 FRED 内核是在干净检出的代码树中构建的。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:695
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `git rev-list` command is used to find the n-number corresponding to a "
"Git hash.  For example:"
msgstr "使用 `git rev-list` 命令查找与 Git 哈希值对应的 N 编号。例如："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:699
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% git rev-list --first-parent --count 031260d64c18 <.>\n"
"247514 <.>\n"
msgstr "% git rev-list --first-parent --count 031260d64c18 <.>\n247514 <.>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:701
#, fuzzy
msgid "git hash to translate (the hash from the above example is reused)"
msgstr "要转换的 Git 哈希值（重用上例中的哈希值）"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:702
#, fuzzy
msgid "The n-number."
msgstr "N 编号。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:708
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Usually this number is not all that important.  However, when bug fixes are "
"committed, this number makes it easy to quickly determine whether the fix is "
"present in the currently running system.  Developers will often refer to the "
"hash of the commit (or provide a URL which has that hash), but not the n-"
"number since the hash is the easily visible identifier for a change while "
"the n-number is not.  Security advisories and errata notices will also note "
"an n-number, which can be directly compared against the system.  When "
"shallow Git clones are used, n-numbers cannot be compared reliably, as the "
"git rev-list command counts all revisions in the repository, which a shallow "
"clone omits."
msgstr "通常，这个编号并不那么重要。但是，提交错误修复后，可以通过这个编号快速确定当前运行的系统是否包含该修复。开发人员通常会提及提交的哈希值（或提供包含该哈希值的 URL），而不是 N 编号，因为哈希值是更容易查看的更改标识符，而 N 编号则不是。安全公告和勘误通知也会注明 N 编号，可直接与系统中的编号进行比较。使用浅克隆 Git 仓库时，无法可靠地比较 N 编号，因为 git rev-list 命令会统计仓库中的所有修订版本，而浅克隆省略了其中一部分。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:710
#, no-wrap
msgid "Updating FreeBSD from Source"
msgstr "从源码更新FreeBSD"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:716
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Updating FreeBSD by compiling from source offers several advantages over "
"binary updates.  Code can be built with options to take advantage of "
"specific hardware.  Parts of the base system can be built with non-default "
"settings, or left out entirely where they are not needed or desired.  The "
"build process takes longer to update a system than just installing binary "
"updates, but allows complete customization to produce a tailored version of "
"FreeBSD."
msgstr ""
"从编译源码来更新FreeBSD比起用Binary更新有几项优点，在编译代码时可以自定义选项"
"来充分运用特定硬件，部份基础系统可以使用非预设的设定值编译，或是在不需要或不"
"想要的时候跳过编译。使用编译的程序来更新系统比起安装Binary来更新会耗时许多，"
"但能够完整自定义一个量身定做版本的FreeBSD。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:718
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr "快速开始"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:722
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This is a quick reference for the typical steps used to update FreeBSD by "
#| "building from source. Later sections describe the process in more detail."
msgid ""
"This is a quick reference for the typical steps used to update FreeBSD by "
"building from source.  Later sections describe the process in more detail."
msgstr ""
"这是从源码编译来更新FreeBSD的标准步骤快速的参考，稍后的章节会更详细的说明这个"
"程序。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:727
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1035
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When switching from man:mergemaster[8] to man:etcupdate[8], the first run "
"might merge changes incorrectly generating spurious conflicts.  To prevent "
"this, perform the following steps *before* updating sources and building the "
"new world:"
msgstr "从 man:mergemaster[8] 切换到 man:etcupdate[8] 时，首次运行可能会错误地合并更改，从而产生不必要的冲突。为避免这种情况，请在更新源代码并构建新系统之前执行以下步骤："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:732
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1040
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# etcupdate extract <.>\n"
"# etcupdate diff <.>\n"
msgstr "# etcupdate extract <.>\n# etcupdate diff <.>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:735
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1043
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Bootstrap the database of stock [.filename]#/etc# files; for more "
"information see man:etcupdate[8]."
msgstr "初始化标准 [.filename]#/etc# 文件的数据库；更多信息请参阅 man:etcupdate[8]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:737
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1045
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Check the diff after bootstrapping. Trim any local changes that are no "
"longer needed to reduce the chance of conflicts in future updates."
msgstr "初始化后检查差异。删除不再需要的本地更改，以降低未来更新时发生冲突的可能性。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:742
msgid "Update and Build"
msgstr "更新并编译"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:756
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# git -C /usr/src pull <.>\n"
"check /usr/src/UPDATING  <.>\n"
"# cd /usr/src          <.>\n"
"# make -j4 buildworld  <.>\n"
"# make -j4 kernel      <.>\n"
"# shutdown -r now      <.>\n"
"# etcupdate -p         <.>\n"
"# cd /usr/src          <.>\n"
"# make installworld    <.>\n"
"# etcupdate -B         <.>\n"
"# shutdown -r now      <.>\n"
msgstr "# git -C /usr/src pull <.>\ncheck /usr/src/UPDATING  <.>\n# cd /usr/src          <.>\n# make -j4 buildworld  <.>\n# make -j4 kernel      <.>\n# shutdown -r now      <.>\n# etcupdate -p         <.>\n# cd /usr/src          <.>\n# make installworld    <.>\n# etcupdate -B         <.>\n# shutdown -r now      <.>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:760
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Get the latest version of the source. See crossref:cutting-edge[updating-src-"
"obtaining-src, Updating the Source] for more information on obtaining and "
"updating source."
msgstr "获取最新版本的源代码。有关获取和更新源代码的更多信息，请参阅 crossref:cutting-edge[updating-src-obtaining-src, 更新源代码]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:762
#, fuzzy
