"upgrade: {\n"
"\turl         = http://ip.of.the.server/FreeBSD:14:amd64/14.3p2\n"
"\tenabled     = yes\n"
"}\n"
msgstr "upgrade: {\n\turl         = http://ip.of.the.server/FreeBSD:14:amd64/14.3p2\n\tenabled     = yes\n}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1467
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"and use it as written above (but use -r upgrade instead of FreeBSD-base)."
msgstr "并按上文所述使用该配置（但使用 -r upgrade，而不是 FreeBSD-base）。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1469
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tracking for Multiple Machines"
msgstr "多部机器追踪"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1475
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When multiple machines need to track the same source tree, it is a waste of "
"disk space, network bandwidth, and CPU cycles to have each system download "
"the sources and rebuild everything.  The solution is to have one machine do "
"most of the work, while the rest of the machines mount that work via NFS.  "
"This section outlines a method of doing so.  For more information about "
"using NFS, refer to crossref:network-servers[network-nfs,\"Network File "
"System (NFS)\"]."
msgstr "多台计算机需要跟踪同一源代码树时，让每台系统都下载源代码并重新构建所有内容，会浪费磁盘空间、网络带宽和 CPU 周期。解决方法是让一台计算机完成大部分工作，其余计算机通过 NFS 挂载这些构建成果。本节介绍一种实现方法。有关使用 NFS 的更多信息，请参阅 crossref:network-servers[network-nfs,\"网络文件系统（NFS）\"]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1480
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First, identify a set of machines which will run the same set of binaries, "
"known as a _build set_.  Each machine can have a custom kernel, but will run "
"the same userland binaries.  From that set, choose a machine to be the "
"_build machine_ that the world and kernel are built on.  Ideally, this is a "
"fast machine that has sufficient spare CPU to run `make buildworld` and "
"`make buildkernel`."
msgstr "首先，确定一组运行相同二进制文件的计算机，称为__构建组__。组内每台计算机都可以使用自定义内核，但运行相同的用户空间二进制文件。从中选择一台计算机作为__构建机__，用于构建 world 和内核。理想情况下，它应是一台速度较快且有足够闲置 CPU 资源的计算机，能够运行 `make buildworld` 和 `make buildkernel`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1484
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Select a machine to be the _test machine_, which will test software updates "
"before they are put into production.  This _must_ be a machine that can "
"afford to be down for an extended period of time.  It can be the build "
"machine, but need not be."
msgstr "选择一台计算机作为__测试机__，用于在软件更新投入生产环境之前进行测试。这台计算机__必须__能够承受较长时间停机。它可以是构建机，但不一定要是。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1487
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"All the machines in this build set need to mount [.filename]#/usr/obj# and [."
"filename]#/usr/src# from the build machine via NFS.  For multiple build "
"sets, [.filename]#/usr/src# should be on one build machine, and NFS mounted "
"on the rest."
msgstr "构建组中的所有计算机都需要通过 NFS 挂载构建机上的 [.filename]#/usr/obj# 和 [.filename]#/usr/src#。如果有多个构建组，[.filename]#/usr/src# 应位于一台构建机上，并通过 NFS 挂载到其余计算机上。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1493
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ensure that [.filename]#/etc/make.conf# and [.filename]#/etc/src.conf# on "
"all the machines in the build set agree with the build machine.  That means "
"that the build machine must build all the parts of the base system that any "
"machine in the build set is going to install.  Also, each build machine "
"should have its kernel name set with `KERNCONF` in [.filename]#/etc/make."
"conf#, and the build machine should list them all in its `KERNCONF`, listing "
"its own kernel first.  The build machine must have the kernel configuration "
"files for each machine in its [.filename]#/usr/src/sys/arch/conf#."
msgstr "确保构建组中所有计算机的 [.filename]#/etc/make.conf# 和 [.filename]#/etc/src.conf# 与构建机一致。这意味着构建机必须构建构建组中任何计算机将要安装的所有基本系统组件。此外，每台构建机都应在 [.filename]#/etc/make.conf# 中通过 `KERNCONF` 设置其内核名称；构建机的 `KERNCONF` 则应列出所有内核，并将自身的内核列在首位。构建机的 [.filename]#/usr/src/sys/arch/conf# 中必须包含每台计算机的内核配置文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1501
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On the build machine, build the kernel and world as described in crossref:"
"cutting-edge[makeworld, Updating FreeBSD from Source], but do not install "
"anything on the build machine.  Instead, install the built kernel on the "
"test machine.  On the test machine, mount [.filename]#/usr/src# and [."
"filename]#/usr/obj# via NFS.  Then, run `shutdown now` to go to single-user "
"mode in order to install the new kernel and world and run `etcupdate` as "
"usual.  When done, reboot to return to normal multi-user operations."
msgstr "在构建机上，按照 crossref:cutting-edge[makeworld, 从源代码更新 FreeBSD]中的说明构建内核和 world，但不要在构建机上安装任何内容。应将构建好的内核安装到测试机上。在测试机上，通过 NFS 挂载 [.filename]#/usr/src# 和 [.filename]#/usr/obj#。然后运行 `shutdown now` 进入单用户模式，以安装新的内核和 world，并照常运行 `etcupdate`。完成后，重新启动以恢复正常的多用户操作。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1504
msgid ""
"After verifying that everything on the test machine is working properly, use "
"the same procedure to install the new software on each of the other machines "
"in the build set."
msgstr ""
"在测试主机上检验完所有东西皆运作正常之后，使用相同的程序将编译好的结果安装到"
"在建置集中的其他主机。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1512
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The same methodology can be used for the ports tree.  The first step is to "
"share [.filename]#/usr/ports# via NFS to all the machines in the build set.  "
"To configure [.filename]#/etc/make.conf# to share distfiles, set `DISTDIR` "
"to a common shared directory that is writable by whichever user `root` is "
"mapped to by the NFS mount.  Each machine should set `WRKDIRPREFIX` to a "
"local build directory, if ports are to be built locally.  Alternately, if "
"the build system is to build and distribute packages to the machines in the "
"build set, set `PACKAGES` on the build system to a directory similar to "
"`DISTDIR`."
msgstr "同样的方法也可用于 ports 树。首先，通过 NFS 将 [.filename]#/usr/ports# 共享给构建组中的所有计算机。要配置 [.filename]#/etc/make.conf# 以共享 distfiles，请将 `DISTDIR` 设置为一个共享目录；NFS 挂载将 `root` 映射到的用户必须对此目录具有写入权限。如果要在本地构建 ports，每台计算机都应将 `WRKDIRPREFIX` 设置为本地构建目录。或者，如果由构建系统构建软件包并分发给构建组中的计算机，请在构建系统上将 `PACKAGES` 设置为类似 `DISTDIR` 的目录。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1514
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Building on non-FreeBSD Hosts"
msgstr "在非 FreeBSD 主机上构建"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1518
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Historically, building required a FreeBSD host.  Nowadays, FreeBSD can be "
"built on Linux and macOS."
msgstr "过去，构建需要使用 FreeBSD 主机。如今，可以在 Linux 和 macOS 上构建 FreeBSD。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1524
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To build on a non-FreeBSD host, the `tools/build/make.py` script is "
"recommended.  This script acts as a wrapper around `bmake`, which is the "
"make implementation used by FreeBSD.  It ensures that the necessary tooling, "
"including the actual FreeBSD's man:make[1], is bootstrapped and that the "
"build environment is properly configured.  In particular, it sets the "
"external toolchain variables, such as `XCC`, `XLD`, and others.  "
"Additionally, the script can pass any additional command arguments, such as "
"`-j 4` for parallel builds or specific make targets, to `bmake`."
msgstr "要在非 FreeBSD 主机上构建，建议使用 `tools/build/make.py` 脚本。该脚本是 FreeBSD 所用 make 实现 `bmake` 的封装。它会确保引导所需的工具，包括实际的 FreeBSD man:make[1]，并正确配置构建环境。具体来说，它会设置 `XCC`、`XLD` 等外部工具链变量。此外，该脚本还可以向 `bmake` 传递其他命令参数，例如用于并行构建的 `-j 4` 或特定的 make 目标。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1529
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A recent version of `bmake` can be used instead of the `tools/build/make.py` "
"script as well.  In that case, however, required environment variables need "
"to be set manually (the easiest way to obtain a list of them is by running "
"`tools/build/make.py --debug`)."
msgstr "也可以使用较新版本的 `bmake`，而不使用 `tools/build/make.py` 脚本。不过，这种情况下需要手动设置所需的环境变量（获取变量列表最简单的方法是运行 `tools/build/make.py --debug`）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1533
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Otherwise, the list of prerequisites for building FreeBSD is rather short.  "
"In fact, it boils down to installing a couple of dependencies."
msgstr "除此之外，构建 FreeBSD 所需的先决条件很少，实际上只需安装几个依赖项。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1536
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On macOS, the only dependency is LLVM.  The necessary dependencies can be "
"installed with package manager (e.g., link:https://brew.sh/[Homebrew]):"
msgstr "在 macOS 上，唯一的依赖项是 LLVM。可以使用软件包管理器（例如 link:https://brew.sh/[Homebrew]）安装所需依赖项："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1540
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "brew install llvm\n"
msgstr "brew install llvm\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1543
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On a Linux distributions, install link:https://clang.llvm.org/[Clang] "
"version 10.0 or newer and the headers for libarchive and libbz2 (often "
"packaged as libarchive-dev and libbz2-dev)."
msgstr "在 Linux 发行版上，安装 link:https://clang.llvm.org/[Clang] 10.0 或更高版本，以及 libarchive 和 libbz2 的头文件（通常打包为 libarchive-dev 和 libbz2-dev）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1545
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once the dependencies are installed, the host should be able to build "
"FreeBSD."
msgstr "安装依赖项后，主机应能够构建 FreeBSD。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1547
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For example, the following `tools/build/make.py` invocation builds the world:"
msgstr "例如，以下 `tools/build/make.py` 调用会构建 world："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1551
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "MAKEOBJDIRPREFIX=/tmp/obj tools/build/make.py -j 8 TARGET=arm64 TARGET_ARCH=aarch64 buildworld\n"
msgstr "MAKEOBJDIRPREFIX=/tmp/obj tools/build/make.py -j 8 TARGET=arm64 TARGET_ARCH=aarch64 buildworld\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1556
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It builds the world for target `aarch64:arm64` on 8 CPUs and uses [."
"filename]#/tmp/obj# for object files.  Note that the variables "
"`MAKEOBJDIRPREFIX`, `TARGET`, and `TARGET_ARCH` are mandatory when building "
"on non-FreeBSD hosts.  Also, make sure to create the object directory "
"pointed to by the `MAKEOBJDIRPREFIX` environment variable."
msgstr "该命令在 8 个 CPU 上为目标 `aarch64:arm64` 构建 world，并使用 [.filename]#/tmp/obj# 存放目标文件。请注意，在非 FreeBSD 主机上构建时，变量 `MAKEOBJDIRPREFIX`、`TARGET` 和 `TARGET_ARCH` 是必需的。此外，请确保创建 `MAKEOBJDIRPREFIX` 环境变量所指向的对象目录。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/cutting-edge/_index.adoc:1557
#, fuzzy
msgid "Refer to man:arch[7] and man:build[7] for more details."
msgstr "更多详情请参阅 man:arch[7] 和 man:build[7]。"

